  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Palantir Technologies has obligated $370M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Palantir Technologies won 91 awards so far, with an average award size of $4.1M, and obligations are up 33.9% year over year. Palantir Technologies saw a multi-year rise in obligations, from $161M in FY21 to $370M in FY26. Palantir Technologies sells mostly software and related services: Software Publishers accounted for $326M and another Software Publishers category accounted for $43.5M, with Computer Systems Design Services at $500K. Palantir Technologies’s largest customers this fiscal year include the Department of Homeland Security at $162M and the Department of Agriculture at $129M. Palantir Technologies also did work for the Department of Veterans Affairs at $22.9M and several other agencies. This profile covers contract obligations through the current fiscal year to date and highlights where federal demand is concentrated.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What is the overall FY2026 to date contract picture for Palantir Technologies?",
        "body": "Palantir Technologies obligated $370M in FY2026 to date across 91 awards, with an average award size of $4.1M. Palantir Technologies’s obligations are up 33.9% year over year, reflecting a step up from $276M in FY25 to $370M in FY26. Software Publishers is the dominant market, with combined entries of $326M and $43.5M, and Computer Systems Design Services is at $500K. Palantir Technologies’s multi-year trend shows steady growth since FY21."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and markets are driving Palantir Technologies’s federal work?",
        "body": "Department of Homeland Security is the largest buyer at $162M, followed by Department of Agriculture at $129M and Department of Veterans Affairs at $22.9M. Department of Transportation, Department of Health and Human Services, and Department of Defense are also buyers at $15.2M, $10.8M, and $8.6M respectively. Software Publishers represents the bulk of obligations, while Computer Systems Design Services is a smaller market. General Services Administration, Department of Energy, Department of the Treasury, and Department of State round out receipts."
      }
    ]
  },
